{"word:hanif":{"id":"word:hanif","title":"Abraham's pure faith","source":"word","note":"A hanif is one who turns from idols to the one God. It is the word for Abraham: \"neither a Jew nor a Christian, but he was a Monotheist, a Muslim\" (3:67).","seeAlso":["Religion","One"],"entries":[{"text":"ḥanīf (حَنِيف): upright, a monotheist. 12 times in 12 verses.","refs":[[141,141],[359,359],[387,387],[617,617],[867,867],[949,949],[1468,1468],[2020,2020],[2023,2023],[2625,2625],[3438,3438],[6134,6134]]}]},"word:hypocrisy":{"id":"word:hypocrisy","title":"Hypocrisy","source":"word","note":"Those who say \"we believe\" and do not. All but one of the verses that use the word are in surahs counted Medinan, where the believers held power.","seeAlso":["Unbelief","Faith"],"entries":[{"text":"munāfiq (مُنافِق): hypocrite. 27 times in 25 verses.","refs":[[553,553],[580,580],[630,630],[632,632],[634,634],[637,637],[1208,1208],[1298,1298],[1301,1302],[1307,1307],[1335,1335],[3350,3350],[3533,3533],[3544,3544],[3556,3556],[3580,3580],[3592,3592],[3605,3605],[4588,4588],[5087,5087],[5188,5188],[5194,5195],[5237,5237]]},{"text":"munāfiqa (مُنافِقَة): hypocrite (woman). 5 times in 5 verses.","refs":[[1301,1302],[3605,3605],[4588,4588],[5087,5087]]},{"text":"nifāq (نِفاق): hypocrisy. 3 times in 3 verses.","refs":[[1311,1311],[1331,1331],[1335,1335]]},{"text":"nāfaqa (نافَقُ): to act the hypocrite. 2 times in 2 verses.","refs":[[459,459],[5136,5136]]}]},"word:hajj":{"id":"word:hajj","title":"The pilgrimage","source":"word","note":"The Hajj to the House at Mecca, \"a duty to God for all who can make the journey\" (3:97), and the lesser visit, the Umrah.","seeAlso":["Prayer","Fasting"],"entries":[{"text":"ḥajj (حَجّ): the pilgrimage. 9 times in 5 verses.","refs":[[195,195],[202,203],[1237,1237],[2621,2621]]},{"text":"ʿumra (عُمْرَة): the visit, the lesser pilgrimage. 2 times in 1 verse.","refs":[[202,202]]},{"text":"shaʿāʾir (شَعائِر): rites, waymarks. 4 times in 4 verses.","refs":[[164,164],[6